{
  "enabled": true,
  "name": "Docs Drift Detect",
  "description": "Manually triggered hook that audits all documentation (docs/*.md and README.md) against the actual codebase, identifies drift, and updates the docs to match the current state of the code.",
  "version": "1",
  "when": {
    "type": "userTriggered"
  },
  "then": {
    "type": "askAgent",
    "prompt": "You are performing a documentation drift detection and correction pass.\n\n## What to do\n\n1. **Read all source code** — every file under LightMeter/ (Logic/, Camera/, Features/, SharedViews/, Design/, ContentView.swift, LightMeterApp.swift) and LightMeterTests/ and Package.swift. Extract: struct/class/enum names, function signatures, published properties, protocol conformances, test counts per file, and UI behavior (buttons, navigation, state transitions).\n\n2. **Read all documentation** — README.md, docs/developer-guide.md, and docs/react-native-handover.md. Extract every factual claim: module descriptions, function names, test counts, capture flow steps, UI element descriptions, architecture diagrams, project structure trees, and cross-references.\n\n3. **Compare code vs docs** — for each doc claim, verify it against the actual code. Look for these drift categories:\n   - **Test counts** — total counts, per-file counts, unit vs property breakdown\n   - **Function signatures** — new/removed/renamed methods, changed parameters\n   - **Published properties** — new @Published vars in view models not mentioned in docs\n   - **UI behavior** — buttons, icons, navigation patterns that changed (e.g. back arrow vs close button)\n   - **Module descriptions** — responsibilities that expanded or changed\n   - **Protocol conformances** — Equatable, Sendable, etc. not mentioned\n   - **Project structure** — files added/removed/moved not reflected in tree diagrams\n   - **Build system** — Package.swift source list vs what docs say is included\n   - **Features not implemented** — docs describing features (like settings gear) that don't exist in code\n   - **Cross-platform references** — react-native-handover.md referencing iOS behavior that changed\n\n4. **Fix every drift** — update the docs to match the code. Be precise: change specific numbers, descriptions, and flow steps. Do not rewrite sections that are already accurate. Preserve the existing document structure, formatting conventions, and style.\n\n5. **Do not touch** docs/light-science-primer.md, docs/github-guide.md, or docs/debugging/ — these don't reference code specifics.\n\n## Rules\n- Code is the source of truth. If docs and code disagree, the docs are wrong.\n- Count tests by counting @Test func declarations, not by guessing.\n- Check UI behavior by reading the actual SwiftUI view code, not by assuming from names.\n- Preserve all markdown formatting conventions (TOC links, mermaid diagrams, table structure).\n- Make minimal targeted edits — don't rewrite paragraphs that are already correct."
  }
}